'''Evan Rikhye''' (born 1971) is an American lawyer who serves as a [[United States federal judge|United States district judge]] for the [[District Court of the Virgin Islands]]. Previously, Rikhye served as an [[assistant United States attorney]] on [[Saint Croix]] from 2008 to 2011 and resumed the role from 2021 to 2024.

==Education==

Rikhye was born in 1971, in [[Boston]], [[Massachusetts]]. He received his [[Bachelor of Arts]] degree in 1993 from [[American University School of International Service]] and his [[Juris Doctor]] from [[American University Washington College of Law]] in 2001.<ref name="Truth Social">{{Cite web|url=https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/116058422580851345|title=Truth Social|website=Truth Social}}</ref><ref name="SJCQ">{{cite web |last=Rikhye |first=Evan |date=February 23, 2026 |title=Senate Judiciary Committee Questionnaire |url=https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/rikhye_sjq.pdf |website=www.judiciary.senate.gov |location=Washington, D.C. |publisher=United States Senate Committee on the Judiciary |access-date=May 18, 2026}}</ref>

==Career==

From 2003 to 2004, Rikhye worked for the [[Federal Election Commission]]. From 2004 to 2006, he worked in the [[United States Department of Justice]] [[Office of Legal Policy]]. From 2006 to 2008, Rikhye worked as an assistant attorney general in the [[United States Department of Justice Civil Rights Division]].<ref name="SJCQ"/> He served as an [[assistant United States attorney]] on [[Saint Croix]] from 2008 to 2011 and again from 2021 to 2024. From 2024 to 2026, Rikhye served as [[senior counsel]] for [[Walmart]] in [[Bentonville, Arkansas]].<ref name="Truth Social"/><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://stthomassource.com/content/2026/02/12/trump-nominates-walmart-senior-counsel-for-v-i-district-court-judgeship/|title=Trump Nominates Walmart Senior Counsel for V.I. District Court Judgeship|date=February 12, 2026}}</ref>

=== District court service ===

On February 12, 2026, President [[Donald Trump]] announced his intention to nominate Rikhye to the seat on the [[District Court of the Virgin Islands]] vacated by Judge [[Wilma A. Lewis]].<ref name="Truth Social"/> On March 2, 2026, Trump formally transmitted Rikhye's nomination to the [[United States Senate]]. On March 25, 2026, the [[United States Senate Committee on the Judiciary|Senate Judiciary Committee]] held a hearing on his nomination. On April 30, 2026, the Senate Judiciary Committee reported his nomination to the floor on a 12–10 [[party-line vote]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.congress.gov/nomination/119th-congress/851/6|title=PN851-6 - Nomination of Evan Rikhye for The Judiciary, 119th Congress (2025-2026)|date=May 14, 2026|website=www.congress.gov}}</ref>  On May 19, 2026, the Senate invoked [[cloture]] on his nomination by a 50–47 vote.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1192/vote_119_2_00128.htm|title=On the Cloture Motion (Motion to Invoke Cloture: Evan Rikhye to be Judge for the District Court of the Virgin Islands)|website=www.senate.gov}}</ref> The following day, the Senate confirmed his nomination by a 52–47 vote.<ref>{{Cite web |date=May 20, 2026 |title=On the Nomination (Confirmation: Evan Rikhye, of the Virgin Islands, to be Judge for the District Court of the Virgin Islands) |url=https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1192/vote_119_2_00130.htm |website=senate.gov}}</ref> He assumed office on May 28, 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |date=May 28, 2026 |title=THE DISTRICT COURT OF THE VIRGIN ISLANDS WELCOMES THE HONORABLE EVAN RIKHYE |url=https://www.vid.uscourts.gov/sites/vid/files/PressRelease004-2026JudgeEvanRikhye.pdf |access-date=June 12, 2026}}</ref>

