'''Harold Dean "Hal" Mooty III''' (born 1983) is an American lawyer who has served as a [[United States federal judge|United States district judge]] of the [[United States District Court for the Northern District of Alabama]] since 2025.

==Early life and education==

Mooty was born in 1983 in [[Tuscaloosa]], [[Alabama]].<ref name="Tuscaloosa">{{Cite web|url=https://www.tuscaloosanews.com/story/news/2025/08/12/trump-nominates-bill-lewis-two-others-to-federal-bench-in-al/85635018007/|title=Trump nominates Bill Lewis, two others to federal bench in AL|first=Marty|last=Roney|website=The Tuscaloosa News}}</ref> He received a [[Bachelor of Science]] degree from the [[University of Alabama]] in 2005, serving as President of the [[Student Government Association]]. He received a [[Juris Doctor]] from the [[University of Alabama School of Law]] in 2008, graduating [[The Order of Barristers]].<ref name="Bradley">{{cite web |last=Mooty III |first=Harold D. |date=August 12, 2025 |title=Harold D. Mooty III Partner |url=https://1npdf11.onenorth.com/pdfrenderer.svc/v1/abcpdf11/GetRenderedPdfByUrl/Mooty%20Harold%20D.pdf/?url=https%3a%2f%2fwww.bradley.com%2fpeople%2fm%2fmooty-harold-d%3fpdf%3d1&attachment=false |website=www.bradley.com |location= |publisher=Bradley Arant Boult Cummings |access-date=August 12, 2025}}</ref><ref name="Questionnaire">{{cite web |last=Mooty III |first=Harold Dean |date=September 3, 2025 |title=Mooty's Senate Judiciary Committee Questionnaire |url=https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/mooty_sjq.pdf |website=www.judiciary.senate.gov |location= |publisher=United States Senate Committee on the Judiciary |access-date=September 3, 2025}}</ref>

==Career==

Mooty was a [[Law firm partner|partner]] at [[Bradley Arant Boult Cummings]] in its [[Huntsville]]  office.<ref name="Bradley"/> He focused on [[commercial litigation]], including [[contracts|contract disputes]], [[shareholder|shareholder disputes]], and [[torts]].  He also practiced [[insurance law|insurance]], [[medical malpractice]], and [[technology law]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.bradley.com/people/m/mooty-harold-d|title=Harold D. Mooty III &#124; People &#124; Bradley|first=Download|last=V-Card|website=www.bradley.com}}</ref><ref name="Questionnaire"/>

===Federal judicial service===

On August 12, 2025, President [[Donald Trump]] announced his intention to nominate Mooty to an unspecified seat on the [[United States District Court for the Northern District of Alabama]].<ref name="Tuscaloosa"/> On September 2, Trump formally nominated Mooty to the seat vacated by Judge [[Abdul K. Kallon]]. A hearing on his nomination was held the next day and his nomination was reported by the [[United States Senate Committee on the Judiciary]] on October 1, 2025 by a 18–4 vote.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Results of the Committee Executive Meeting|url=https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/download/2025-10-01_ebm_resultspdf?download=1|website=United States Senate Committee on the Judiciary|access-date=December 17, 2025}}</ref> On October 16, [[cloture]] was invoked on his nomination by a 62–34 vote.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1191/vote_119_1_00574.htm|title=On the Cloture Motion (Motion to Invoke Cloture: Harold D. Mooty III to be U.S. District Judge for the Northern District of Alabama)|date=October 16, 2025|website=www.congress.gov}}</ref> On October 21, his nomination was confirmed by a 66–32 vote.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 21, 2025 |title=On the Nomination (Confirmation: Harold D. Mooty III, of Alabama, to be U.S. District Judge for the Northern District of Alabama) |url=https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1191/vote_119_1_00577.htm |access-date=October 21, 2025 |website=senate.gov}}</ref> He received his judicial commission on October 21 and he was sworn into office on October 22 by Senior Judge [[Charles Lynwood Smith Jr.]]<ref>{{Cite web |date=November 4, 2025 |title=RE: WELCOME TO TWO NEW U.S. DISTRICT JUDGES |url=https://www.alnd.uscourts.gov/sites/alnd/files/Public%20Notice%20-%20Welcome%20New%20Judges%20%28FINAL%2004NOV25%29.pdf |access-date=November 7, 2025 |website=United States District Court for the Northern District of Alabama}}</ref>

