'''James Russell Sweeney II''' (born 1961) is the [[United States federal judge|chief United States district judge]] of the [[United States District Court for the Southern District of Indiana]].

== Biography ==

Sweeney received a [[Bachelor of Science]], with merit, in 1983 from the [[United States Naval Academy]]. From 1983 to 1992 Sweeney was an active duty [[Naval Flight Officer]] in the [[United States Marine Corps]]. He received a [[Juris Doctor]], ''magna cum laude'', in 1996 from [[Notre Dame Law School]]. Sweeney then [[law clerk|clerked]] for Judge [[John Daniel Tinder]] of the [[United States District Court for the Southern District of Indiana]] and Judge [[James L. Ryan]] of the [[United States Court of Appeals for the Sixth Circuit]]. In 1999, Sweeney joined the [[Indianapolis]] law firm [[Barnes & Thornburg]] as an [[Associate attorney|associate]] and was promoted to [[Partner (business rank)|partner]] in 2005,<ref>{{cite web | url=https://vettingroom.org/tag/james-sweeney/ | title=James Sweeney | date=January 5, 2018 }}</ref> where he practiced [[corporate law]] and [[Civil law (legal system)|civil law]] until becoming a judge in 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/presidential-actions/president-donald-j-trump-announces-nomination-indiana-attorney-james-sweeney-fill-judicial-emergency/|via=[[NARA|National Archives]]|work=[[whitehouse.gov]]|title=President Donald J. Trump Announces Nomination of Indiana Attorney James Sweeney to Fill Judicial Emergency}}</ref>

== Federal judicial service ==

His nomination was announced and sent to the [[United States Senate|Senate]] on November 1, 2017.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.einpresswire.com/article/413125246/president-donald-j-trump-announces-nomination-of-indiana-attorney-james-sweeney-to-fill-judicial-emergency|title=President Donald J. Trump Announces Nomination of Indiana Attorney James Sweeney to Fill Judicial Emergency|last= |first= |date=November 1, 2017|website=EIN Presswire|publisher=IPD Group|access-date=November 2, 2017|quote=}}</ref> President Trump nominated Sweeney to the seat on the [[United States District Court for the Southern District of Indiana]] vacated by Judge [[Sarah Evans Barker]], who assumed [[senior status]] on June 30, 2014. A hearing on his nomination before the [[United States Senate Committee on the Judiciary|Senate Judiciary Committee]] was held on January 10, 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/meetings/01/10/2018/nominations|title=United States Senate Committee on the Judiciary|website=www.judiciary.senate.gov|date=January 10, 2018 }}</ref> On February 8, 2018, the Judiciary Committee voted to report his nomination by [[voice vote]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.washingtonexaminer.com/senate-judiciary-committee-approves-four-trump-judicial-nominations/article/2648523|title=Senate Judiciary Committee approves four Trump judicial nominations|first=Melissa|last=Quinn|date=February 8, 2018|publisher=}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/Results%20of%20Executive%20Business%20Meeting%2002-08-18.pdf|title=Results of Executive Business Meeting – February 8, 2018, Senate Judiciary Committee|publisher=}}</ref> On August 28, 2018, his nomination was confirmed by [[voice vote]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.congress.gov/nomination/115th-congress/1198|title=PN1198 — James R. Sweeney II — The Judiciary|last=|first=|date=November 1, 2017|website=[[United States Senate]]|access-date=August 28, 2018|language=en}}</ref> He received his judicial commission on September 13, 2018.<ref>{{FJC Bio|nid=5153451|inline=yes}}</ref> He was sworn in on September 24, 2018.<ref>{{Cite press release|date=September 24, 2018|title=James R. Sweeney II sworn in as United States District Judge|url=https://www.insd.uscourts.gov/sites/insd/files/JRS%20sworn%20in%20press%20release.pdf|website=insd.uscourts.gov|access-date=May 28, 2023}}</ref> He became the chief judge on July 11, 2025.<ref>{{Cite press release|date=July 11, 2025|title=Hon. James R. Sweeney II Named Chief Judge|url=https://www.insd.uscourts.gov/sites/insd/files/JRS%20chief%20judge%20PR%20FINAL.pdf|website=insd.uscourts.gov|access-date=July 17, 2025}}</ref>

