'''John Thomas Shepherd''' (born 1987) is an American lawyer who has served as a [[United States federal judge|United States district judge]] of the [[United States District Court for the Western District of Arkansas]] since 2026. He previously served as a judge of the [[Arkansas Circuit Courts|Arkansas 13th Judicial State Circuit Court]] in [[El Dorado, Arkansas]] from 2025 to 2026.

==Early life and education==

Shepherd was born in 1987 in [[El Dorado, Arkansas]].<ref name="SJQ">{{cite web |last=Shepherd |first=John Thomas |date=February 4, 2026 |title=Senate Judiciary Committee Questionnaire |url=https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/shepherd_sjq.pdf |website=www.judiciary.senate.gov |location= |publisher=United States Senate Committee on the Judiciary |access-date=February 6, 2026}}</ref> He received his [[Bachelor of Arts]] degree in 2009 from [[Rice University]] and his [[Juris Doctor]], ''[[magna cum laude]]''  in 2013 from [[University of Arkansas School of Law]].<ref name="Truth Social">{{Cite web|url=https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/115850515035074475|title=Truth Social|website=Truth Social}}</ref> During his time at Rice, he played [[quarterback]] for the [[Rice Owls football]] team.<ref name="SJQ" /><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/170296/john-thomas-shepherd|title=John Thomas Shepherd - Rice Owls Quarterback|website=ESPN}}</ref>

==Career==

From 2025 to 2026, Shepherd has served as a judge of the [[Arkansas Circuit Courts|Arkansas 13th Judicial State Circuit Court]] in [[El Dorado, Arkansas]]. He previously served as a prosecuting attorney in the same circuit.<ref name="SJQ" /><ref name="Truth Social"/>

=== Federal judicial service ===

On January 6, 2026, President [[Donald Trump]] announced his intention to nominate Shepherd to an unspecified seat on the [[United States District Court for the Western District of Arkansas]].<ref name="Truth Social"/> On January 29, 2026, Trump formally nominated Shepherd to the seat on the Western District of Arkansas being vacated by Judge [[Susan O. Hickey]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.congress.gov/nomination/119th-congress/787/3|title=PN787-3 - Nomination of John Thomas Shepherd for The Judiciary, 119th Congress (2025-2026)|date=January 29, 2026|website=www.congress.gov}}</ref> On February 4, 2026, a hearing on his nomination was held before the [[United States Senate Committee on the Judiciary|Senate Judiciary Committee]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=February 4, 2026 |title=Nominations {{!}} United States Senate Committee on the Judiciary |url=https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/committee-activity/hearings/nominations-02-04-2026 |website=www.judiciary.senate.gov |language=en}}</ref> On March 5, 2026, his nomination was reported from the Judiciary Committee by a 12–10 [[party-line vote]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=March 5, 2026 |title=Results of Executive Business Meeting  |url=https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/0eb50502-98e6-61ed-bd12-2132806a72a9/20260305_EBM_Results.pdf |website=U.S. Senate Committee on the Judiciary}}</ref> On April 13, 2026 the Senate invoked [[cloture]] by a 50–44 vote.<ref>{{Cite web |date=April 13, 2026 |title=On the Cloture Motion (Motion to Invoke Cloture: John Thomas Shepherd to be U.S. District Judge for the Western District of Arkansas) |url=https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1192/vote_119_2_00075.htm |website=U.S. Senate}}</ref> The following day, the Senate confirmed his nomination in a 53–46 vote.<ref>{{Cite web |date=April 14, 2026 |title=On the Nomination (Confirmation: John Thomas Shepherd, of Arkansas, to be U.S. District Judge for the Western District of Arkansas) |url=https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1192/vote_119_2_00076.htm |website=U.S. Senate}}</ref> He received his judicial commission on April 23, 2026.<ref>{{FJC Bio|nid=13762120|inline=yes}}</ref>

