'''Martin Karl Reidinger''' (born December 18, 1958) is the [[United States federal judge|chief United States district judge]] of the [[United States District Court for the Western District of North Carolina]]. 

==Education and career==

Born in [[New Haven, Connecticut|New Haven]], [[Connecticut]], Reidinger received a [[Bachelor of Arts]] degree from the [[University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill]] in 1981 and a [[Juris Doctor]] from the [[University of North Carolina School of Law]] in 1984. He practiced as a civil litigator at Adams, Hendon, Carson, Crow & Saenger in [[Asheville, North Carolina|Asheville]] from 1984 to 2007.<ref name="govinfo">{{cite web |url=https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CRECB-2007-pt17/html/CRECB-2007-pt17-Pg24001.htm |title=Congressional Record |publisher=[[GovInfo]] | access-date=April 16, 2026 | archive-date=April 16, 2026 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260416165921/https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CRECB-2007-pt17/html/CRECB-2007-pt17-Pg24001.htm | url-status=live}}</ref>

==Federal judicial service==

President [[George W. Bush]] first nominated Reidinger to a seat on the [[United States District Court for the Western District of North Carolina]], vacated by [[Graham Calder Mullen]], on September 29, 2006.<ref name="fjc">{{cite web |url=https://www.fjc.gov/history/judges/reidinger-martin-karl |title=Reidinger, Martin Karl |publisher=[[Federal Judicial Center]] | access-date=April 16, 2026 | archive-date=March 23, 2026 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260323183621/https://www.fjc.gov/history/judges/reidinger-martin-karl | url-status=live}}</ref> The nomination did not receive a Senate vote before end of the congressional session, with Bush renominating Reidinger on January 9, 2007. Reidinger was confirmed by the [[United States Senate]] on September 10, 2007, and received his commission on September 12, 2007. He became chief judge on June 2, 2020.

==Personal life==

Reidinger is married, has four children, and lives in [[Asheville, North Carolina]].<ref name="govinfo"/>

