'''Megan Blair Benton'''<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://apps.calbar.ca.gov/attorney/Licensee/Detail/273749|title=Megan Blair Benton # 273749 - Attorney Licensee Search|website=apps.calbar.ca.gov}}</ref> (born 1985) is an American lawyer who has served as a [[United States federal judge|United States district judge]] of the [[United States District Court for the Western District of Missouri]] since 2026. She was previously a judge of [[Missouri Circuit Courts|Missouri's 6th Judicial Circuit]] from 2021 to 2026.

==Early life and education==

Benton is the daughter of [[Duane Benton]], a judge on the [[United States Court of Appeals for the Eighth Circuit]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Raymond |first=Nate |date=November 14, 2025 |title=Trump taps former Thomas clerk, transgender sports foe for judgeships |url=https://www.reuters.com/legal/government/trump-taps-former-thomas-clerk-transgender-sports-foe-judgeships-2025-11-14/ |url-status=live |access-date=November 20, 2026 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> She received [[Bachelor of Arts]] and [[Master of Arts]] degrees from [[Emory University]]. She received a [[Juris Doctor]] from the [[Vanderbilt University Law School]].<ref name="TS">{{Cite web|url=https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/115549907135940696|title=Truth Social|website=Truth Social}}</ref><ref name="MoJudges">{{Cite web|url=https://yourmissourijudges.org/judges/megan-benton-2024/|title=Megan Benton 2024}}</ref>

==Career==

Benton served as a prosecuting attorney in the [[Platte County, Missouri|Platte County]] prosecutor's office. From 2021 to 2026, she was a judge of [[Missouri Circuit Courts|Missouri's 6th Judicial Circuit]], which covers the same county.<ref name="TS"/><ref name="MoJudges"/> She was appointed by [[Missouri Governor]] [[Mike Parson]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://themissouritimes.com/parson-appoints-megan-benton-as-associate-circuit-judge-for-the-6th-judicial-circuit/|title=Parson appoints Megan Benton as associate circuit judge for the 6th Judicial Circuit|first=Press|last=Release|date=May 7, 2021}}</ref>

===Federal judicial service===

On November 14, 2025, President [[Donald Trump]] announced his intention to nominate Benton to a seat on the [[United States District Court for the Western District of Missouri]] to be vacated by Judge [[M. Douglas Harpool]].<ref name="TS"/>  On December 17, 2025, the [[U.S. Senate Judiciary Committee]] held a hearing on her nomination.<ref>{{cite web | title=Nominations &#124; United States Senate Committee on the Judiciary | url=https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/committee-activity/hearings/nominations-12-17-2025 }}</ref> On January 15, 2026 the committee advanced her nomination by a 12–10 vote.<ref>{{Cite web |date=January 15, 2026 |title=Results of Executive Business Meeting |url=https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/2fcac5c2-f9d7-49b6-b87e-e45639bb2108/2026-01-15_EBM_Results.pdf |access-date=February 12, 2026 |website=U.S. Senate Judiciary Committee}}</ref> On February 4, the Senate invoked [[cloture]] on her nomination by a 51–47 vote.<ref>{{Cite web |date=February 4, 2026 |title=On the Cloture Motion (Motion to Invoke Cloture: Megan Blair Benton to be U.S. District Judge for the Western District of Missouri) |url=https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1192/vote_119_2_00027.htm |access-date=February 12, 2026 |website=senate.gov}}</ref> Later that day, her nomination was confirmed by a 51–46 vote.<ref>{{Cite web |date=February 4, 2026 |title=On the Nomination (Confirmation: Megan Blair Benton, of Missouri, to be U.S. District Judge for the Western District of Missouri) |url=https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1192/vote_119_2_00028.htm |access-date=February 12, 2026 |website=senate.gov}}</ref> She received her judicial commission on February 10, 2026.<ref>{{FJC Bio|nid=13762107|inline=yes}}</ref>

