'''Robert James Jonker''' (born March 9, 1960) is a [[United States federal judge|United States district judge]] for the [[United States District Court for the Western District of Michigan|Western District of Michigan]], where he served as chief judge from 2015 to 2022.

==Education and career==

Born in [[Holland, Michigan]], Jonker received a [[Bachelor of Arts]] degree from [[Calvin College]] in 1982 and a [[Juris Doctor]] from the [[University of Michigan Law School]] in 1985. He was a [[law clerk]] for Judge [[John F. Feikens]] of the United States District Court for the Eastern District of Michigan, from 1985 to 1987. He practiced commercial and environmental law at [[Warner Norcross & Judd]], a [[Grand Rapids, Michigan|Grand Rapids]]-based firm, from 1987 to 2007.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.crainsgrandrapids.com/news/robert-jonker-grand-rapids-200-2023/ |title=Robert Jonker |date=October 30, 2023 |publisher=[[Crain_Communications#Crain's_Grand_Rapids_Business|Crain's Grand Rapids Business]] | access-date=April 16, 2026 | archive-date=May 11, 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240511113620/https://www.crainsgrandrapids.com/news/robert-jonker-grand-rapids-200-2023/ | url-status=live}}</ref>

==Federal judicial service==

President [[George W. Bush]] first nominated Jonker to a seat on the [[United States District Court for the Western District of Michigan]], vacated by [[Gordon Jay Quist]], in 2006, but the nomination was returned to the president at the end of the congressional session without a Senate vote. Bush resubmitted the nomination on March 19, 2007. Jonker was confirmed by the [[United States Senate]] on July 9, 2007, and received his commission on July 16, 2007. He served as chief judge from July 18, 2015 to July 17, 2022<ref>{{Cite web |title=Robert James Jonker {{!}} United States Courts |url=https://www.uscourts.gov/judicial-milestones/robert-james-jonker |access-date=2023-12-12 |website=www.uscourts.gov |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fjc.gov/history/courts/u.s.-district-courts-districts-michigan-chief-judges |title=U.S. District Courts for the Districts of Michigan: Chief Judges |publisher=[[Federal Judicial Center]] | access-date=April 16, 2026 | archive-date=October 7, 2025 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251007111232/https://www.fjc.gov/history/courts/u.s.-district-courts-districts-michigan-chief-judges | url-status=live}}</ref>

