'''Bobby Ed Shepherd''' (born 1951)<ref name="Hearing">{{cite web |url=https://www.congress.gov/109/chrg/CHRG-109shrg32199/CHRG-109shrg32199.pdf|title=Hearing before the Committee on the Judiciary|work=United States Senate|date=June 28, 2006}}</ref>{{rp|101}} is a [[United States federal judge|United States circuit judge]] of the [[United States Court of Appeals for the Eighth Circuit]]. He maintains chambers in [[El Dorado, Arkansas|El Dorado]], the seat of [[Union County, Arkansas|Union County]] in south Arkansas.

== Education ==
Shepherd received a [[Bachelor of Arts]] degree from [[Ouachita Baptist University]] in Arkadelphia in 1973. He received his [[Juris Doctor]] from the [[University of Arkansas School of Law]] in [[Fayetteville, Arkansas|Fayetteville]] in 1975.{{r|Hearing|p=101}}

== Career==
Shepherd was a [[United States magistrate judge]] for the [[United States District Court for the Western District of Arkansas]] from 1993 until he joined the Eighth Circuit. His appointment was only the second time ever a sitting magistrate judge had been elevated directly to a federal court of appeals. From 1991 to 1993, Shepherd was an Arkansas state trial judge for the [[Arkansas Circuit Courts|13th Judicial Circuit]], in the southern end of the state. Previously, Shepherd had been in private practice as an attorney in Arkansas from 1976 to 1990.{{r|Hearing|p=101}}

[[File:United States Court of Appeals for the Eighth Circuit - 2010.jpg|thumb|right|250px|United States Court of Appeals for the Eighth Circuit in 2010]]

=== Federal judicial service ===

Shepherd was nominated to the Eighth Circuit{{r|Hearing|p=61}} by President [[George W. Bush]] on May 18, 2006, to fill a seat to be vacated by Judge [[Morris S. Arnold]]. Shepherd was confirmed by the [[United States Senate]] by [[voice vote]] on July 20, 2006.<ref>{{Cite web |title=PN1593 — Bobby E. Shepherd — The Judiciary |url=https://www.congress.gov/nomination/109th-congress/1593/ |access-date=June 20, 2023}}</ref> He received his commission on October 10, 2006.<ref>{{FJC Bio|nid=1392471|inline=yes}}</ref>

On July 20, 2026, Shepherd announced that he would be taking [[Senior Status]].<ref>{{Cite web | title=Bush-appointee Eighth Circuit Judge Bobby Shepherd to take senior status after successor confirmed {{!}} Just The News | url=https://justthenews.com/government/courts-law/bush-appointee-eighth-circuit-judge-bobby-shepherd-take-senior-status-after | access-date=2026-09-01 | website=justthenews.com}}</ref>

== Personal life ==

Shepherd's son [[Matthew Shepherd]], has served as  a state representative in the [[Arkansas House of Representatives]] since 2011 and as the [[Speaker of the Arkansas House of Representatives]] since 2018.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.arkansasonline.com/news/2018/jul/22/new-speaker-takes-helm-in-house-2018072-1/|title=New state House speaker takes helm, faces choppy seas in addressing ethics issues|date=July 22, 2018|website=Arkansas Online}}</ref>

